{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>Provide yourselves men, etc.</b> At first he made it dependent upon Israel themselves, that they would be appointed from among them, and afterward he said: ״וַאֲשִׂימֵם בְּרָאשֵׁיכֶם״ — which implies that they would be appointed by Moses. And further, what is the meaning of the בֵּי״ת of ״בְּרָאשֵׁיכֶם״? For he should have said: ״וַאֲשִׂימֵם רָאשֵׁיכֶם״. And our Sages of blessed memory interpreted (Sifrei 13) that the guilt of the people hangs upon their heads. But one must explain this according to the plain sense. And I say: the heads that he mentioned are not the judges, but rather the princes of the tribes. And Moses said: You have it in your power to appoint judges who will rule over your tribes, but you do not have the power to give them authority over the princes as well — only I do. Therefore he said: You — provide yourselves men, etc., for your tribes, so that they will rule over all your tribes; and I will set them also over your heads — so that they will rule even over the princes, who are your heads."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :kli-yakar, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:11:00.430114699Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}